ble/disable and cleanup ACs → E020/E040;\nFIPS check-payload ACs → E014/E015; AgentRuntime label-application AC → E040 (E2E over the\ndeployed operator); dashboard agent-list AC → E030; disconnected-install AC → E021/E040;\nminimal-image-contract documentation MUST → E050. Runtime discovery/registration ACs at the top\nof the strategy describe upstream operator behavior explicitly tracked out of scope\n(RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589) and are validated, not built, by this decomposition (E040).\n\n## Investigation Handling of Strategy Unknowns\n\n| Strategy unknown | Disposition |\n| --- | --- |\n| Upstream kagenti-operator functional with all three controllers? (open question) | E001 Investigation — outcome can add remediation work (BRANCH-A-E016) or force TP scope reduction. |\n| Does the operator require Keycloak as a runtime dependency; can ClientRegistrationController be disabled for TP? (open question) | Folded into E001 — resolved by the same experiment (exercising the upstream operator) and the same deliverable (gap analysis). |\n| Minimal image contract for TP: A2A protocol format or simpler metadata format? (open question) | Technical half folded into E001 (what the operator actually consumes); documentation half is E050 content. Does not change which epics exist. |\n| Which AuthBridge sidecar variants are needed for TP? (open question) | E002 Investigation — main plan ships the strategy's committed minimum (`authbridge-proxy`); additional variants are conditional BRANCH-B-E017. |\n| Dashboard integration depth: tab vs standalone navigation? (open question) | E003 Investigation — gates E030 scope (`rewrite`). |\n| What happens to user-namespace AgentRuntime CRs when the component is disabled? (open question) | E004 Investigation — gates E020 cleanup scope (`rewrite`). |\n| Midstream fork set up and synced (assumption, needs validation) | E010/E011 — the repo-onboarding epics' own deliverable. |\n| AgentRuntime CRD schema stable enough for TP (assumption, needs validation) | E001 (CRD stability assessment). |\n| RBAC coexistence in `redhat-ods-applications` (assumption, needs validation) | E040 E2E coverage + E020 AC; risk-table mitigation. |\n| OTEL trace sink MUST from parent RFE under team discussion (Open note on ACs) | Health warning — not in this strategy's scope or ACs; would add scope if confirmed. |\n\n## Component Mapping (canonical Jira components)\n\n| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| kagenti-operator | Agentic | No kagenti-specific canonical component exists; all Kagenti-team epics (forks, license scans, Konflux onboarding, remediation) map to `Agentic`. |\n| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | Same mapping; separate epics because they are separate strategy components/repos. |\n| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | Closest canonical name for the core platform operator repo (paired with `AI Core Dashboard` below). |\n| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Direct match. |\n| QE (no owned component) | QE | Direct match. |\n| Docs (no owned component) | Documentation | Direct match. |\n\nNew-component detection: neither kagenti-operator nor kagenti-extensions has an architecture\ncontext file (only a tangential RBAC mention of `mcp.kagenti.com` in odh-dashboard.md), so both\nget the full Rule 20 onboarding chain (repo-onboarding + license-validation in parallel →\nkonflux-onboarding). No general implementation epic follows the chain: the strategy explicitly\nexcludes operator runtime development, so the chain's consumer is the rhods-operator component\ncontroller (E020), which references manifests and image digests as configuration (ACs, not edges).\n\n## Conditional Branches\n\n- **BRANCH-A-E016** (gated by E001, `add_remediation`): activated only if the upstream\n  validation finds functional gaps. If gaps exceed two sprints of effort, the fallback is TP\n  scope reduction (defer MLflowReconciler and/or ClientRegistrationController) per the\n  strategy's risk mitigation, not full remediation.\n- **BRANCH-B-E017** (gated by E002, `remove`): activated only if TP requires AuthBridge\n  variants beyond `authbridge-proxy`. If TP ships proxy-only, the epic is dropped and the\n  variants defer to a later release.\n\nBranch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **OTEL trace sink (open scope risk):** the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) carries a MUST for\n  OTEL trace sink integration \"not yet reflected here — under team discussion\". If confirmed,\n  it adds scope beyond this decomposition (observability wiring was otherwise delegated to\n  RHAIRFE-7589/ARC). Track the discussion outcome before release planning.\n- **Process gates pending human review:** Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, Licence\n  Validation, UXD Support, and Documentation Support are all \"Pending human review\" in the\n  strategy's prerequisites table, and the issue carries `ac-review-pending` and\n  `confidence-yellow` labels. The proposed acceptance criteria themselves are marked\n  \"requires PM/Engineering validation\".\n- **Konflux lead time (schedule risk, not an AC):** pipeline capacity \"needs submission\" and\n  late submission risks the code-complete deadline. The onboarding request must be submitted\n  immediately (tracked in E014/E015 scope and risks); escalation path per the strategy risk\n  table (platform lead if <2 weeks before deadline).\n- **Minor strategy typo:** proposed AC 3 references CRD `agentrimes.agent.kagenti.dev`\n  (should be the AgentRuntime CRD name as defined upstream, `agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`).\n- **Priority note:** the dashboard HLR is P1 while the operator productization is P0 —\n  consistent with the strategy's TP framing (dashboard is \"basic visibility\" only). No\n  inversion detected. P2 multi-arch is correctly opportunistic.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable. Both external dependencies (upstream kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions)\nalready exist in the `kagenti` GitHub or