{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-faddf718-5c00-4e7e-a1e8-87a5760eb1fc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa45ac35e59d695c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b80poyxr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E001.md","content":"# Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness for Tech Preview\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves whether the upstream kagenti-operator (in the `kagenti` GitHub org) is functional and stable enough to productize for Tech Preview without additional development work. The strategy's effort estimate (L) and epic structure assume a working upstream operator; if gaps exist, remediation work must be added upstream-first and the effort may shift to XL, or TP scope may need reduction. The deliverable is a gap analysis document with a go/no-go recommendation and, if gaps are found, a scoped remediation plan.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Validate that all three upstream controllers exist and function as described in architecture context overlay 0014:\n  - `AgentRuntimeReconciler`, including metadata fetch from the workload's `/.well-known/agent-card.json` endpoint via mTLS, stored inline in `AgentRuntime.Status.Card`\n  - `MLflowReconciler`\n  - `ClientRegistrationController`\n- Determine whether the `ClientRegistrationController` requires Keycloak as a runtime dependency, and whether it can be disabled for Tech Preview (Keycloak deployment and OAuth2 infrastructure are managed outside this strategy)\n- Assess the stability of the AgentRuntime CRD schema (`agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`) for Tech Preview — CRD field changes after productization require migration\n- Determine the minimal image contract the operator actually enforces (does it require the A2A protocol card format, or accept a simpler metadata format?) — this defines the endpoint format, health check, and card structure that Tech Preview documentation must describe\n- Produce a gap analysis document containing: per-controller pass/fail against the criteria above, the Keycloak dependency answer with evidence, a CRD breaking-change risk rating, the validated image contract, and a recommendation — proceed as planned, remediate (with a scoped effort estimate), or reduce TP scope (defer `MLflowReconciler` and/or `ClientRegistrationController`, per the strategy's risk mitigation if gaps exceed two sprints of work)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A gap analysis document exists that records a pass/fail result for each of the three controllers against the overlay 0014 inventory, with evidence\n- The Keycloak runtime-dependency question is answered with evidence, including whether the `ClientRegistrationController` can be disabled for Tech Preview\n- The AgentRuntime CRD schema is assessed with a breaking-change risk rating for Tech Preview\n- The metadata format the operator consumes (A2A card vs simpler format) is documented, including endpoint format, health check expectations, and card structure\n- A recommendation is recorded: proceed / remediate (with effort estimate) / reduce TP scope — and if remediation is recommended, the remediation scope is enumerated\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nNo HLR is directly delivered by this investigation. It de-risks the assumptions underlying the\nP0 HLRs (Konflux-built operator images, DSC component enablement) by validating the upstream\ndependency the strategy marks \"critical, must validate in sprint 1\", and it feeds the\nminimal-image-contract documentation requirement (strategy-level MUST acceptance criterion).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63252,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba13640ea0c9c49d","agent_id":"a13c4baab7f592a79","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"7502d838-a910-41ac-b3f9-5788bb2d494f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:11:57.247Z","sub