{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2c885605-02c5-45c0-b3cd-482c1c5fe2fd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbdcf505dd0aef0d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b80poyxr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E002.md","content":"# Determine the AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation decides which AuthBridge sidecar image variants ship in Tech Preview. Upstream kagenti-extensions provides three variants — `authbridge-proxy` (full proxy, default mode), `authbridge-envoy` (Envoy ext_proc mode), and `authbridge-lite` (auth-only) — and each variant requires its own Konflux component. The strategy commits only to `authbridge-proxy` as the minimum viable set for TP; whether the other variants are needed for the 3.5 release is an open product question owned jointly by the Kagenti team and PM. The deliverable is a recorded decision that fixes the Konflux onboarding scope.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Decide, with PM input, whether Tech Preview ships `authbridge-proxy` only, or also includes `authbridge-envoy` and/or `authbridge-lite`\n- For each additional variant included, define the Konflux component scope (same FIPS/UBI9 recipe as the proxy variant) and the `RELATED_IMAGE_*` CSV entries it requires\n- Record the decision with rationale, including the deferral plan for any variant excluded from TP\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A decision record exists naming the exact AuthBridge variant set for Tech Preview, with PM sign-off and rationale\n- If variants beyond `authbridge-proxy` are included, the per-variant Konflux component scope is enumerated; if excluded, the deferral (later release) is recorded\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nNo HLR is directly delivered. This investigation fixes the scope of the P1 HLR \"AuthBridge\nproxy sidecar image built via Konflux with FIPS compliance\" and determines whether a