{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-482001ac-a235-4a05-b4a8-046cde6ba07b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b68bd773b5ea82f6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b80poyxr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E004.md","content":"# Define AgentRuntime cleanup semantics when the kagenti component is disabled\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation decides what happens to user-created AgentRuntime CRs in user namespaces when the kagenti-operator component is disabled in the Data Science Cluster CR (`managementState: Removed`). The component controller's standard cleanup covers operator-managed resources in `redhat-ods-applications` (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration, namespace-scoped resources), but user-created CRs in other namespaces may become orphaned. The open question is whether the cleanup should include cross-namespace CRD deletion or whether orphan semantics are documented instead. The answer changes the cleanup/finalizer scope of the component controller implementation. The deliverable is a documented cleanup-semantics decision consistent with the platform's garbage-collection pattern.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Determine the behavior of user-created AgentRuntime CRs in user namespaces when the component transitions to `Removed` (operator no longer running to reconcile them)\n- Decide the cleanup scope: operator-managed resources only (with documented orphan behavior for user CRs) vs cleanup that also enumerates and deletes user-created CRs cross-namespace (e.g., via an explicit finalizer on the component CR)\n- Survey the cleanup and finalizer patterns of the existing component controllers in the rhods-operator component registry for precedent\n- Record the decision with rationale, including the resource-cleanup inventory (controller Deployment; ClusterRoles/ClusterRoleBindings/Roles/RoleBindings; the AgentRuntime CRD; the mutating webhook configuration; ConfigMaps/Secrets in `redhat-ods-applications`)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A decision record exists fixing the disable-cleanup semantics (operator-managed-only vs including user-created CRs), with rationale grounded in existing component-controller precedent\n- The full cleanup inventory is enumerated, matching the strategy's resource-cleanup non-functional requirement\n- If cross-namespace cleanup is chosen, a finalizer design outline is included; if not, the documented orphan behavior for user CRs is specified\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nNo HLR is directly delivered. This investigation fixes the scope of the P0 HLR \"When disabled\n(`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed resources are cleaned up\".\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65193,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba13640ea0c9c49d","agent_id":"a13c4baab7f592a79","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"7a92ca42-d01d-4727-9be2-49feffac6fd8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:12:24.226Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006 into epics"}
