{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-08ae5eb1-46fd-4072-a478-8cc32aa1e3c3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0450d7929e7c8ab","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b80poyxr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E014.md","content":"# Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic onboards the kagenti-operator container image to the Konflux build pipeline, making a FIPS-compliant, UBI9-based image available for the platform to deploy. It converts the upstream Dockerfile to the standard RHOAI Go-operator multi-stage pattern and takes the image through Konflux `check-payload` FIPS validation. Because pipeline onboarding has lead time and the strategy flags it as the critical-path schedule risk, the onboarding request must be submitted immediately and tracked against the code-complete deadline.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Submit the Konflux onboarding request for a new component building from the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork, and track it against the release code-complete deadline (escalate to the platform lead if submission is delayed past two weeks before the deadline, per the strategy risk table)\n- Convert the Dockerfile to the multi-stage pattern used by rhods-operator, model-registry-operator, and other RHOAI Go operators: builder stage compiles with FIPS flags (`CGO_ENABLED=1`, `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`); production stage copies the binary onto `ubi9/ubi-minimal`\n- Add `rpms.lock.yaml` for RPM lockfile pinning and `go.sum` for Go dependency locking\n- Apply the platform container security pattern: non-root execution (`USER 65532:65532` following the distroless convention), capability dropping (`capabilities.drop: [\"ALL\"]`), `seccompProfile.type: RuntimeDefault`\n- Configure AMD64 builds as required for Tech Preview; include arm64 only if the pipeline supports it without additional effort\n- Validate that the built image passes Konflux `check-payload` for FIPS compliance (binary linked against OpenSSL, no statically-linked Go crypto)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A Konflux component exists for the kagenti-operator image, built from the midstream fork, with a green build pipeline\n- The image passes Konflux `check-payload` validation for FIPS compliance\n- The Dockerfile follows the multi-stage FIPS pattern on a UBI9 base, with `rpms.lock.yaml` and `go.sum` present in the build context\n- The container security requirements (non-root, dropped capabilities, RuntimeDefault seccomp) are satisfied in the image and manifests\n- An AMD64 image is produced; arm64 status is recorded (included if free, otherwise deferred with rationale)\n- The SHA256-pinned image reference is published for consumption by OLM/CSV packaging\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation (`GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`, `CGO_ENABLED=1`) on UBI9 base (RFE acceptance criterion)\n- [P2] Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required for TP; arm64 if pipeline supports it without additional effort)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67956,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba13640ea0c9c49d","agent_id":"a13c4baab7f592a79","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"1e6a4763-9089-47c9-8b99-6c574ae34568","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:13:09.547Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006 into epics"}
