{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ab293323-378b-4a1e-9829-949780cee845","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc3c84b3354bd726","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b80poyxr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E020.md","content":"# KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic registers kagenti-operator as a new standard component in the rhods-operator Data Science Cluster (DSC) control plane, following the established 16-component pattern. It delivers the `KagentiOperator` component CRD, the component controller with the standard action pipeline, DSC CR schema extension, and kustomize manifest integration from the midstream fork. The component defaults to `Removed` (Tech Preview opt-in), and supports full resource cleanup on disable per the resolved cleanup semantics.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define a new `KagentiOperator` component CRD in the `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, following the pattern of `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, `FeastOperator`, and the other existing component CRDs\n- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize, releases, kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect) and register it in `internal/controller/components/registry/` so the DSC controller manages it\n- Extend the DSC CR schema with the kagenti-operator component field\n- Implement `managementState` lifecycle: `Managed` (deploy operator + CRDs + RBAC + webhook) and `Removed` (delete the controller Deployment, all RBAC, the AgentRuntime CRD, the mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources in `redhat-ods-applications`), per the documented cleanup-semantics decision for user-created AgentRuntime CRs\n- Integrate kustomize manifests pulled from the kagenti-operator midstream fork at pinned commits via `get_all_manifests.sh`, stored under `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`, with RHOAI-specific overlays for namespace, image references, and RBAC adjustments\n- Deploy the kagenti-operator into `redhat-ods-applications`, consistent with the other platform component operators; the operator watches all namespaces for AgentRuntime CRs\n- Default the component to `Removed` (explicit opt-in for Tech Preview) so existing clusters are unaffected by RHOAI upgrade\n- Verify RBAC coexistence of the kagenti-operator alongside other platform operators in `redhat-ods-applications`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with DSC configured with kagenti-operator `managementState: Managed`, when the DSC controller reconciles, then the kagenti-operator Deployment is created in `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image — measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator` returning a Ready deployment\n- Given the component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the component controller reconciles, then all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration, namespace-scoped resources) are deleted — measured by the deployment query returning no results and the AgentRuntime CRD returning \"not found\" — and the documented cleanup semantics for user-created AgentRuntime CRs are enforced\n- The component defaults to `Removed` in DSC (TP opt-in); an upgrade of an existing cluster without explicit opt-in leaves the cluster unchanged\n- The Konflux build pipeline for the kagenti-operator image is green and a SHA256-pinned image digest is available to reference in the deployment and CSV (build pipeline green gate)\n- The kagenti-operator manifests are available from the midstream fork at a pinned commit (configuration reference gate)\n- License clearance for the kagenti-operator image has been recorded (license validation gate)\n- The kagenti-operator runs in `redhat-ods-applications` without RBAC conflicts with the other platform operators\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard component controller pattern with `managementState: Managed/Removed` (RFE acceptance criterion)\n- [P0] When disabled (`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed resources are cleaned up: controller Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, namespace-scoped resources (RFE acceptance criterion)\n- [P0] Tech Preview maturity level with explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) (RFE acceptance criterion)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":69504,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba13640ea0c9c49d","agent_id":"a13c4baab7f592a79","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"28f1c1ee-79a5-4d1e-bcf5-77815bc52d54","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:13:35.514Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006 into epics"}
