Given the odh-dashboard is deployed with the kagenti BFF plugin enabled (feature flag active), when a user navigates to the agent views section, then the dashboard displays a list of AgentRuntime CRs from the user's accessible namespaces — measured by the dashboard rendering AgentRuntime data retrieved via the BFF API proxy\n- Given the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in DSC, the dashboard hides all agent-related UI elements\n- The BFF sidecar port assignment is verified collision-free against the current Module Federation port allocations\n- The agent list view implements the resolved UX design direction (integration depth per the PM/UX decision)\n- The feature flag and component-state gating behave correctly across DSC state transitions\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag for agent views (RFE acceptance criterion)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71155,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba13640ea0c9c49d","agent_id":"a13c4baab7f592a79","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"acf8726b-9036-4977-b794-d8462a217c20","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:13:55.678Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006 into epics"}
