{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-510ee5fa-087a-4559-b0ac-a41ee862b941","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b03a50f79d746291","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b80poyxr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E040.md","content":"# E2E test plan and validation for the kagenti component lifecycle\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the QE test plan and E2E test suite for the kagenti-operator component: DSC lifecycle (Managed/Removed), resource cleanup including multi-namespace scenarios, mutating-webhook ordering interactions, deployed-operator runtime acceptance criteria, and disconnected-installation validation. It verifies the productization work end to end.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Create the test plan covering component lifecycle, cleanup, webhook ordering, and disconnected installation\n- Develop E2E tests for the component lifecycle: `Managed` deployment readiness, `Managed`→`Removed` cleanup of all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration) per the documented cleanup semantics, including resources spread across multiple namespaces\n- Develop E2E coverage for the deployed operator's acceptance behavior: creating an AgentRuntime CR referencing an existing Deployment results in the `kagenti.io/type: agent` label being applied to the target workload\n- Test mutating-webhook ordering explicitly: the kagenti AuthBridge injection webhook (`reinvocationPolicy: IfNeeded`) combined with other platform mutating webhooks (HardwareProfile, connection injection); if conflicts arise, record and verify explicit `webhookOrder` annotations\n- Validate disconnected installation: image mirroring with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` resolution, operator and AuthBridge images running from the mirrored registry\n- Verify the finalizer-based cleanup (if cross-namespace cleanup was chosen in the cleanup-semantics decision) enumerates and deletes all owned resources\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A test plan document exists covering component lifecycle, cleanup (multi-namespace), webhook ordering, and disconnected validation\n- The E2E suite runs the Managed/Removed lifecycle scenarios and they pass, including cleanup of resources in multiple namespaces\n- The AgentRuntime label-application acceptance scenario passes against the deployed operator\n- Webhook-ordering scenarios (kagenti injection webhook alongside HardwareProfile and connection-injection webhooks) pass, with any ordering remediation recorded\n- Disconnected-installation validation is executed with recorded results (images resolved from the mirror registry via `RELATED_IMAGE_*`)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nNo numbered HLR covers QE directly. This epic verifies the P0 HLRs (DSC enable/disable, Removed\ncleanup, TP opt-in), the P1 OLM/CSV disconnected-installation HLR, and the strategy's measurable\nacceptance criteria for the deployed operator.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71889,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba13640ea0c9c49d","agent_id":"a13c4baab7f592a79","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"05ba7a5b-3998-46cd-bd0f-7d921a398d5f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:14:05.614Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006 into epics"}
