{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-df6dd389-1f32-4d2c-8bfc-9b885ac89c25","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa8813791bd954ce","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b80poyxr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E050.md","content":"# Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the agent image contract\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic authors the customer-facing documentation for the kagenti-operator Tech Preview: installation and upgrade documentation for enabling the component via the Data Science Cluster CR, and the minimal image contract documentation that tells customers how to build a discoverable agent image. This is substantive new content authoring in the Red Hat docs content process, and it runs last so the docs describe what was actually built.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline (to be authored inside the Red Hat docs toolchain):\n\n- **Enabling the kagenti-operator (installation):** how to enable the component via the DSC CR (`managementState: Managed`), the Tech Preview opt-in default (`Removed`), what gets deployed (operator, CRDs, RBAC, webhook in `redhat-ods-applications`), and how to disable it (`managementState: Removed`) with the resulting resource cleanup behavior, including the documented behavior of user-created AgentRuntime CRs\n- **Minimal agent image contract:** how to build an agent image any framework can use — the capability description endpoint format (per the validated metadata format the operator consumes), health check expectations, and card structure (endpoint, health check, card fields), based on the upstream validation findings\n- **Onboarding an agent:** creating an AgentRuntime CR that selects an existing Deployment (targetRef selection), and what the platform then does (registration, discoverability, console visibility) at Tech Preview scope\n- **Disconnected installation:** mirroring the kagenti-operator and AuthBridge images for air-gapped clusters via the `RELATED_IMAGE_*` mechanism\n- **Upgrade notes:** TP maturity caveats and the absence of backwards-compatibility concerns (new component, disabled by default)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Installation and enablement documentation covers DSC-based enablement and disablement, including the cleanup behavior on disable\n- The minimal image contract documentation covers endpoint format, health check, and card structure, matching the validated contract the operator enforces\n- Agent onboarding documentation covers AgentRuntime CR creation via targetRef selection\n- Disconnected-installation documentation covers image mirroring via `RELATED_IMAGE_*`\n- All content is technically reviewed against the implementation before publication\n- Content is published through the Red Hat docs content process for the Tech Preview release\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nNo numbered HLR covers documentation. This epic delivers the strategy-level MUST acceptance\ncriterion \"Documentation covers the minimal image contract for creating a discoverable agent\n(endpoint format, health check, card structure)\" and the Docs team commitment (installation and\nupgrade documentation for enabling kagenti-operator via DSC).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72574,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba13640ea0c9c49d","agent_id":"a13c4baab7f592a79","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"02cd81b2-996a-45e6-9432-5fd9c68803b7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:14:16.927Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006 into epics"}
