{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f003b5c0-5446-473d-9845-2d3ef73e8cc8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0d7f8100a35f6d8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b80poyxr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-A-E016.md","content":"# Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps for Tech Preview\n\n## Description\n\nThis conditional epic exists only if the upstream kagenti-operator validation finds functional gaps. It closes the identified gaps — missing or broken controllers (AgentRuntimeReconciler including the agent-card metadata fetch, MLflowReconciler, ClientRegistrationController), AgentRuntime CRD schema defects, or image-contract mismatches — in the upstream `kagenti/*` repositories first (upstream-first policy), then syncs the fixes into the `opendatahub-io` midstream fork so the Konflux-built images and pinned manifests pick them up.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the remediation items enumerated in the upstream validation gap analysis, developed in the upstream `kagenti/kagenti-operator` repository first and then pulled into the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork\n- Re-run the validation criteria from the gap analysis against the remediated operator\n- Rebaseline the pinned midstream fork commit and rebuild the affected images so downstream productization consumes the fixed operator\n- If the gap analysis recommends TP scope reduction instead of full remediation (gaps exceeding two sprints of effort), implement the agreed reduction (e.g., defer MLflowReconciler and/or ClientRegistrationController, disable the Keycloak-dependent controller) rather than closing the gaps\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- All gap-analysis remediation items are implemented upstream and synced to the midstream fork, or the agreed TP scope reduction is implemented and recorded\n- The remediated (or scope-reduced) operator passes the validation criteria from the gap analysis\n- The midstream fork pinned commit is rebaselined and the affected images rebuilt\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Upstream-first policy: significant changes go to `kagenti/*` repos before being pulled into `opendatahub-io/*` midstream forks (RFE acceptance criterion)\n- Supports the P0 Konflux-built operator image and DSC component HLRs by ensuring the productized operator is functional\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":73298,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba13640ea0c9c49d","agent_id":"a13c4baab7f592a79","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"ba2cf4da-1b29-4138-814d-8d8f5aac1f13","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:14:26.387Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006 into epics"}
