{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84c61e3b01de1371","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness for Tech Preview\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness for Tech Preview\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves whether the upstream kagenti-operator (in the `kagenti` GitHub org) is functional and stable enough to productize for Tech Preview without additional development work. The strategy's effort estimate (L) and epic structure assume a working upstream operator; if gaps exist, remediation work must be added upstream-first and the effort may shift to XL, or TP scope may need reduction. The deliverable is a gap analysis document with a go/no-go recommendation and, if gaps are found, a scoped remediation plan.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Validate that all three upstream controllers exist and function as described in architecture context overlay 0014:\n34\t  - `AgentRuntimeReconciler`, including metadata fetch from the workload's `/.well-known/agent-card.json` endpoint via mTLS, stored inline in `AgentRuntime.Status.Card`\n35\t  - `MLflowReconciler`\n36\t  - `ClientRegistrationController`\n37\t- Determine whether the `ClientRegistrationController` requires Keycloak as a runtime dependency, and whether it can be disabled for Tech Preview (Keycloak deployment and OAuth2 infrastructure are managed outside this strategy)\n38\t- Assess the stability of the AgentRuntime CRD schema (`agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`) for Tech Preview — CRD field changes after productization require migration\n39\t- Determine the minimal image contract the operator actually enforces (does it require the A2A protocol card format, or accept a simpler metadata format?) — this defines the endpoint format, health check, and card structure that Tech Preview documentation must describe\n40\t- Produce a gap analysis document containing: per-controller pass/fail against the criteria above, the Keycloak dependency answer with evidence, a CRD breaking-change risk rating, the validated image contract, and a recommendation — proceed as planned, remediate (with a scoped effort estimate), or reduce TP scope (defer `MLflowReconciler` and/or `ClientRegistrationController`, per the strategy's risk mitigation if gaps exceed two sprints of work)\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A gap analysis document exists that records a pass/fail result for each of the three controllers against the overlay 0014 inventory, with evidence\n45\t- The Keycloak runtime-dependency question is answered with evidence, including whether the `ClientRegistrationController` can be disabled for Tech Preview\n46\t- The AgentRuntime CRD schema is assessed with a breaking-change risk rating for Tech Preview\n47\t- The metadata format the operator consumes (A2A card vs simpler format) is documented, including endpoint format, health check expectations, and card structure\n48\t- A recommendation is recorded: proceed / remediate (with effort estimate) / reduce TP scope — and if remediation is recommended, the remediation scope is enumerated\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\tNo HLR is directly delivered by this investigation. It de-risks the assumptions underlying the\n53\tP0 HLRs (Konflux-built operator images, DSC component enablement) by validating the upstream\n54\tdependency the strategy marks \"critical, must validate in sprint 1\", and it feeds the\n55\tminimal-image-contract documentation requirement (strategy-level MUST acceptance criterion).\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2cde650df82e178","agent_id":"aa5a2bc1ebccaf2b6","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"6a0fdb42-e041-4e22-be5e-2ba00a1a9e02","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:19:20.571Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84c61e3b01de1371","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
