{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aab54a8b0043ef66","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E030\n3\ttitle: Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the decided integration depth is a standalone navigation section\n15\t    rather than a tab in an existing project view, the BFF/UI scope expands (~2 sprints\n16\t    vs ~1) and the epic is rewritten to that scope.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers the Tech Preview dashboard integration for agent visibility: a feature flag in the OdhDashboardConfig CR that gates agent views on the DSC component state, a new Go BFF container registered via Module Federation that proxies Kubernetes API requests for AgentRuntime CR management, and a basic read-only agent list view. Full agent management UI is out of scope for Tech Preview; the integration depth (tab in an existing project view vs standalone navigation section) follows the resolved UX decision.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Add a `disableKagenti` feature flag (or equivalent) to the `OdhDashboardConfig` CR, gated by the DSC component state: when the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in DSC, the dashboard hides all agent-related UI elements\n43\t- Implement a new Go BFF container following the pattern of `gen-ai-ui`, `maas-ui`, and the other federated modules, proxying requests to the Kubernetes API for AgentRuntime CR management\n44\t- Run the BFF as a sidecar container in the dashboard pod on the next available port in the 8043-8743 range, verified against the current assignments (8043-model-registry, 8143-gen-ai, 8243-maas, 8343-mlflow, 8443-eval-hub, 8543-automl, 8643-autorag) to avoid collisions\n45\t- Register the kagenti dashboard plugin via the odh-dashboard Module Federation architecture\n46\t- Implement the TP agent list view per the resolved integration depth and UX design direction: list AgentRuntime CRs from the user's accessible namespaces, show status, link to workload details (read-only)\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given the odh-dashboard is deployed with the kagenti BFF plugin enabled (feature flag active), when a user navigates to the agent views section, then the dashboard displays a list of AgentRuntime CRs from the user's accessible namespaces — measured by the dashboard rendering AgentRuntime data retrieved via the BFF API proxy\n51\t- Given the kagenti-operator component is `Removed` in DSC, the dashboard hides all agent-related UI elements\n52\t- The BFF sidecar port assignment is verified collision-free against the current Module Federation port allocations\n53\t- The agent list view implements the resolved UX design direction (integration depth per the PM/UX decision)\n54\t- The feature flag and component-state gating behave correctly across DSC state transitions\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P1] Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag for agent views (RFE acceptance criterion)\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2cde650df82e178","agent_id":"aa5a2bc1ebccaf2b6","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"7d74ed5b-bdab-42a