{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-948b6bdba44edeb5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E040\n3\ttitle: E2E test plan and validation for the kagenti component lifecycle\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: QE\n6\tteam: QE\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E020\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E021\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 0\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 5\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# E2E test plan and validation for the kagenti component lifecycle\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the QE test plan and E2E test suite for the kagenti-operator component: DSC lifecycle (Managed/Removed), resource cleanup including multi-namespace scenarios, mutating-webhook ordering interactions, deployed-operator runtime acceptance criteria, and disconnected-installation validation. It verifies the productization work end to end.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Create the test plan covering component lifecycle, cleanup, webhook ordering, and disconnected installation\n40\t- Develop E2E tests for the component lifecycle: `Managed` deployment readiness, `Managed`→`Removed` cleanup of all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration) per the documented cleanup semantics, including resources spread across multiple namespaces\n41\t- Develop E2E coverage for the deployed operator's acceptance behavior: creating an AgentRuntime CR referencing an existing Deployment results in the `kagenti.io/type: agent` label being applied to the target workload\n42\t- Test mutating-webhook ordering explicitly: the kagenti AuthBridge injection webhook (`reinvocationPolicy: IfNeeded`) combined with other platform mutating webhooks (HardwareProfile, connection injection); if conflicts arise, record and verify explicit `webhookOrder` annotations\n43\t- Validate disconnected installation: image mirroring with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` resolution, operator and AuthBridge images running from the mirrored registry\n44\t- Verify the finalizer-based cleanup (if cross-namespace cleanup was chosen in the cleanup-semantics decision) enumerates and deletes all owned resources\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- A test plan document exists covering component lifecycle, cleanup (multi-namespace), webhook ordering, and disconnected validation\n49\t- The E2E suite runs the Managed/Removed lifecycle scenarios and they pass, including cleanup of resources in multiple namespaces\n50\t- The AgentRuntime label-application acceptance scenario passes against the deployed operator\n51\t- Webhook-ordering scenarios (kagenti injection webhook alongside HardwareProfile and connection-injection webhooks) pass, with any ordering remediation recorded\n52\t- Disconnected-installation validation is executed with recorded results (images resolved from the mirror registry via `RELATED_IMAGE_*`)\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\tNo numbered HLR covers QE directly. This epic verifies the P0 HLRs (DSC enable/disable, Removed\n57\tcleanup, TP opt-in), the P1 OLM/CSV disconnected-installation HLR, and the strategy's measurable\n58\tacceptance criteria for the deployed operator.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2cde650df82e178","agent_id":"aa5a2bc1ebccaf2b6","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"84db5202-c8fd-4a32-a226-03e4f1f54c95","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:19:33.343Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-948b6bdba44edeb5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"co