 Preview opt-in default (`Removed`), what gets deployed (operator, CRDs, RBAC, webhook in `redhat-ods-applications`), and how to disable it (`managementState: Removed`) with the resulting resource cleanup behavior, including the documented behavior of user-created AgentRuntime CRs\n51\t- **Minimal agent image contract:** how to build an agent image any framework can use — the capability description endpoint format (per the validated metadata format the operator consumes), health check expectations, and card structure (endpoint, health check, card fields), based on the upstream validation findings\n52\t- **Onboarding an agent:** creating an AgentRuntime CR that selects an existing Deployment (targetRef selection), and what the platform then does (registration, discoverability, console visibility) at Tech Preview scope\n53\t- **Disconnected installation:** mirroring the kagenti-operator and AuthBridge images for air-gapped clusters via the `RELATED_IMAGE_*` mechanism\n54\t- **Upgrade notes:** TP maturity caveats and the absence of backwards-compatibility concerns (new component, disabled by default)\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Installation and enablement documentation covers DSC-based enablement and disablement, including the cleanup behavior on disable\n59\t- The minimal image contract documentation covers endpoint format, health check, and card structure, matching the validated contract the operator enforces\n60\t- Agent onboarding documentation covers AgentRuntime CR creation via targetRef selection\n61\t- Disconnected-installation documentation covers image mirroring via `RELATED_IMAGE_*`\n62\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implementation before publication\n63\t- Content is published through the Red Hat docs content process for the Tech Preview release\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\tNo numbered HLR covers documentation. This epic delivers the strategy-level MUST acceptance\n68\tcriterion \"Documentation covers the minimal image contract for creating a discoverable agent\n69\t(endpoint format, health check, card structure)\" and the Docs team commitment (installation and\n70\tupgrade documentation for enabling kagenti-operator via DSC).\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2cde650df82e178","agent_id":"aa5a2bc1ebccaf2b6","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"8ee99ba6-480d-4eae-93e5-dbf2cb5be78b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:19:34.077Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9acc445057a8ea32","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
