ope strategy items are covered: Konflux onboarding for both image families (E014/E015 +\n136\tBRANCH-B for the variant expansion), component controller integration (E020), CSV packaging\n137\t(E021), dashboard BFF + feature flag (E030), QE (E040), documentation (E050), plus the full Rule 20\n138\tonboarding chain for the two components lacking architecture context files. All seven proposed\n139\tstrategy ACs are mapped (1/3→E020, 2→E040, 4/5→E014/E015, 6→E030, 7→E021/E040). The top-level\n140\truntime MUST ACs (discovery, metadata sync, degraded condition, sandbox registration) are\n141\texplicitly traced out of scope to RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589 with E040 validating the deployed\n142\tbehavior — matching the strategy's own scope statement. Both conditional branches cover their\n143\tbounded outcomes including fallbacks (TP scope reduction for E001; proxy-only deferral for E002).\n144\tStrategy-level context is carried forward, not dropped: every open question has a recorded\n145\tdisposition, and the OTEL trace-sink risk, pending process gates, Konflux lead time, and the\n146\t`agentrimes` CRD typo all appear in Health Warnings. Documentation Support requirement is met by\n147\tthe E050 docs-authoring epic, correctly placed last per Rule 11.\n148\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b6a284e22c088e1","agent_id":"abe58463e2c7d19d1","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"005a6358-6cec-4a05-8b4e-eae95679f240","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:25:33.106Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84086b9e3e68591b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
