{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2e92dfc5e0b6d60","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 15\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n10\t\n11\tStrategy triage: **full decomposition** (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy is\n12\tL-effort (6-9 sprints), spans four strategy components (kagenti-operator, kagenti-extensions,\n13\trhods-operator, odh-dashboard) and five teams (Kagenti, Platform / ODH Operator, Dashboard, QE,\n14\tDocs). No Staff Engineer Input overrides (section contains template placeholder text only).\n15\t\n16\tThe strategy productizes an existing upstream operator: build-pipeline onboarding, DSC component\n17\tcontroller integration, OLM/CSV packaging, and dashboard BFF registration. Runtime agent\n18\tbehavior (registration, discovery, metadata sync) is explicitly out of scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589).\n19\t\n20\t## Epic List\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n23\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine the AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Determine TP dashboard integration depth for agent views | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Define AgentRuntime cleanup semantics when the kagenti component is disabled | Investigation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | Establish the kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | Establish the kagenti-extensions midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | License validation for kagenti-operator and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | License validation for kagenti-extensions and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P1 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 | Konflux build onboarding for the AuthBridge proxy sidecar image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E020 | KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E021 | OLM/CSV packaging for kagenti-operator with disconnected-install support | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E030 | Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E040 | E2E test plan and validation for the kagenti component lifecycle | Implementation | QE | P1 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E050 | Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the agent image contract | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P0 |\n39\t\n40\tBranch (conditional) epics — not standalone main-plan nodes; attached to their gating\n41\tInvestigation as plan documents:\n42\t\n43\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Gated by |\n44\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-A-E016 | Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps for Tech Preview | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E017 | Konflux onboarding for additional AuthBridge sidecar variants | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P2 | RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 |\n47\t\n48\t## Dependency DAG\n49\t\n50\t```mermaid\n51\tgraph TD\n52\t    E001[\"E001 Upstream kagenti validation (Inv)\"]\n53\t    E002[\"E002 AuthBridge variant set (Inv)\"]\n54\t    E003[\"E003 Dashboard depth (Inv)\"]\n55\t    E004[\"E004 Cleanup semantics (Inv)\"]\n56\t    E010[\"E010 repo-onboarding kagenti-operator\"]\n57\t    E011[\"E11 repo-onboarding kagenti-extensions\"]\n58\t    E012[\"E012 license-validation kagenti-operator\"]\n59\t    E013[\"E013 license-validation kagenti-extensions\"]\n60\t    E014[\"E014 Konflux onboarding kagenti-operator image\"]\n61\t    E015[\"E015 Konflux onboarding AuthBridge proxy image\"]\n62\t    E020[\"E020 KagentiOperator DSC component controller\"]\n63\t    E021[\"E021 OLM/CSV packaging\"]\n64\t    E030[\"E030 Dashboard BFF plugin + feature flag\"]\n65\t    E040[\"E040 QE E2E lifecycle + disconnected validation\"]\n66\t    E050[\"E050 Documentation (docs-authoring)\"]\n67\t\n68\t    E010 --> E014\n69\t    E011 --> E015\n70\t    E004 --> E020\n71\t    E020 --> E021\n72\t    E003 --> E030\n73\t    E020 --> E040\n74\t    E021 --> E040\n75\t    E001 --> E050\n76\t    E010 --> E050\n77\t    E011 --> E050\n78\t    E012 --> E050\n79\t    E013 --> E050\n80\t    E014 --> E050\n81\t    E015 --> E050\n82\t    E020 --> E050\n83\t    E021 --> E050\n84\t    E030 --> E050\n85\t    E040 --> E050\n86\t\n87\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E016 Upstream gap remediation (conditional)\"]\n88\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E017 Additional AuthBridge variants (conditional)\"]\n89\t    E001 -.-> BA\n90\t    E002 -.-> BB\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\tSolid edges are main-plan dependencies (dependency must complete before dependent starts).\n94\tDashed edges are conditional branch activations: the branch epic exists only if the gating\n95\tInvestigation resolves to the outcome that requires it.\n96\t\n97\t## DAG Justification\n98\t\n99\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n100\t| --- | --- | --- |\n101\t| E010 → E014 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux component builds from the opendatahub-io midstream fork; the pipeline needs the repo. |\n102\t| E011 → E015 | Rule 5 | Same: the AuthBridge proxy image builds from the kagenti-extensions midstream fork. |\n103\t| E004 → E020 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementation) | Whether component cleanup includes cross-namespace CRD deletion or documents orphan semantics changes the controller's cleanup/finalizer scope. Bounded outcome → `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on E020. |\n104\t| E020 → E021 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The CSV declares the `KagentiOperator` CRD and the component controller's RBAC — artifacts produced by the controller work; packaging builds against them. |\n105\t| E003 → E030 | Rule 3 | Agent-list-as-tab (~1 sprint) vs standalone navigation section (~2 sprints) changes the BFF/UI scope of the dashboard epic. `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on E030. |\n106\t| E020 → E040 | Rule 13 | E2E lifecycle tests exercise the component controller's Managed/Removed behavior. |\n107\t| E021 → E040 | Rule 13 | Disconnected validation exercises the CSV `RELATED_IMAGE_*` mirroring path. |\n108\t| all Implementations → E050 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every main-plan Implementation epic. E001 is additionally included because the image-contract documentation content depends on its outcome. Docs priority derived from strategy `priority: Critical` → P0 (docs-authoring priority exception; does not push P0 upstream). |\n109\t| E001 -.-> BRANCH-A-E016 | Rule 3 (conditional branch, add_remediation) | If the upstream operator has functional gaps, remediation work is added upstream-first. |\n110\t| E002 -.-> BRANCH-B-E017 | Rule 3 (conditional branch, remove) | If TP requires more than the authbridge-proxy variant, additional Konflux components are added. |\n111\t\n112\tDeliberately absent edges (anti-patterns per the rules):\n113\t\n114\t| Non-edge | Rule | Rationale |\n115\t| --- | --- | --- |\n116\t| E012/E013 → E014/E015 | Rules 7-8 | License validation runs in parallel with Konflux onboarding (independent inputs). |\n117\t| E014/E015 → E020/E021 | Rules 10, 13 | SHA256-pinned image digests consumed by the CSV (`RELATED_IMAGE_*`) are configuration references, not build-against artifacts — enforced as \"pinned digest available / pipeline green\" ACs on E020/E021, never as DAG edges. Konflux onboarding and the component controller must run in parallel. |\n118\t| E001 → E014 | Rule 14 + strategy risk direction | The strategy directs submitting the Konflux onboarding request immediately (lead-time risk) while upstream validation runs in sprint 1; the pipeline onboards whatever code exists at pinned commits. The validation outcome gates only the conditional remediation branch. |\n119\t| E020 → E030 | Rule 14 | Different repos with no shared build-against artifact: the dashboard BFF reads the upstream-defined AgentRuntime CRD and DSC component state (configuration references); coupling is enforced by an AC on E030, not an edge. |\n120\t| E010 → E020 | Rules 13-14 | The controller consumes midstream manifests at pinned commits — a configuration reference, gated by an AC on E020, not an edge. |\n121\t\n122\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n123\t\n124\t| HLR | Priority | Covering epics |\n125\t| --- | --- | --- |\n126\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 base | P0 | E014 (chain: E010, E012) |\n127\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern, `managementState: Managed/Removed` | P0 | E020 |\n128\t| When disabled (`Removed`), all operator-managed resources cleaned up | P0 | E020 (scope resolved by E004) |\n129\t| Upstream-first policy (changes land in `kagenti/*` before `opendatahub-io/*` midstream) | P0 | E010, E011 (sync process ACs); BRANCH-A-E016 if remediation is triggered |\n130\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E020 |\n131\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag | P1 | E030 (depth