{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f3b0189c472f525","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E020\n3\ttitle: KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the resolved cleanup semantics require cross-namespace deletion\n15\t    of user-created AgentRuntime CRs (finalizer-based enumeration), the controller\n16\t    cleanup scope is rewritten to include it; if operator-managed-only is chosen,\n17\t    orphan behavior is documented instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic registers kagenti-operator as a new standard component in the rhods-operator Data Science Cluster (DSC) control plane, following the established 16-component pattern. It delivers the `KagentiOperator` component CRD, the component controller with the standard action pipeline, DSC CR schema extension, and kustomize manifest integration from the midstream fork. The component defaults to `Removed` (Tech Preview opt-in), and supports full resource cleanup on disable per the resolved cleanup semantics.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Define a new `KagentiOperator` component CRD in the `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1` group, following the pattern of `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, `FeastOperator`, and the other existing component CRDs\n44\t- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize, releases, kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect) and register it in `internal/controller/components/registry/` so the DSC controller manages it\n45\t- Extend the DSC CR schema with the kagenti-operator component field\n46\t- Implement `managementState` lifecycle: `Managed` (deploy operator + CRDs + RBAC + webhook) and `Removed` (delete the controller Deployment, all RBAC, the AgentRuntime CRD, the mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources in `redhat-ods-applications`), per the documented cleanup-semantics decision for user-created AgentRuntime CRs\n47\t- Integrate kustomize manifests pulled from the kagenti-operator midstream fork at pinned commits via `get_all_manifests.sh`, stored under `prefetched-manifests/kagenti-operator/`, with RHOAI-specific overlays for namespace, image references, and RBAC adjustments\n48\t- Deploy the kagenti-operator into `redhat-ods-applications`, consistent with the other platform component operators; the operator watches all namespaces for AgentRuntime CRs\n49\t- Default the component to `Removed` (explicit opt-in for Tech Preview) so existing clusters are unaffected by RHOAI upgrade\n50\t- Verify RBAC coexistence of the kagenti-operator alongside other platform operators in `redhat-ods-applications`\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with DSC configured with kagenti-operator `managementState: Managed`, when the DSC controller reconciles, then the kagenti-operator Deployment is created in `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image — measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator` returning a Ready deployment\n55\t- Given the component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the component controller reconciles, then all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration, namespace-scoped resources) are deleted — measured by the deployment query returning no results and the AgentRuntime CRD returning \"not found\" — and the documented cleanup semantics for user-created AgentRuntime CRs are enforced\n56\t- The component defaults to `Removed` in DSC (TP opt-in); an upgrade of an existing cluster without explicit opt-in leaves the cluster unchanged\n57\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the kagenti-operator image is green and a SHA256-pinned image digest is available to reference in the deployment and CSV (build pipeline green gate)\n58\t- The kagenti-operator manifests are available from the midstream fork at a pinned commit (configuration reference gate)\n59\t- License clearance for the kagenti-operator image has been recorded (license validation gate)\n60\t- The kagenti-operator runs in `redhat-ods-applications` without RBAC conflicts with the other platform operators\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- [P0] Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard component controller pattern with `managementState: Managed/Removed` (RFE acceptance criterion)\n65\t- [P0] When disabled (`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed resources are cleaned up: controller Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, namespace-scoped resources (RFE acceptance criterion)\n66\t- [P0] Tech Preview maturity level with explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) (RFE acceptance criterion)\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b6a284e22c088e1","agent_id":"abe58463e2c7d19d1","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"eb337151-0f81-4d80-81a7-d407862f68d5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:25:50.588Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f3b0189c472f525","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAIS