{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98e3cbfe5c4c1e61","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E014\n3\ttitle: Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: konflux-onboarding\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic onboards the kagenti-operator container image to the Konflux build pipeline, making a FIPS-compliant, UBI9-based image available for the platform to deploy. It converts the upstream Dockerfile to the standard RHOAI Go-operator multi-stage pattern and takes the image through Konflux `check-payload` FIPS validation. Because pipeline onboarding has lead time and the strategy flags it as the critical-path schedule risk, the onboarding request must be submitted immediately and tracked against the code-complete deadline.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Submit the Konflux onboarding request for a new component building from the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork, and track it against the release code-complete deadline (escalate to the platform lead if submission is delayed past two weeks before the deadline, per the strategy risk table)\n39\t- Convert the Dockerfile to the multi-stage pattern used by rhods-operator, model-registry-operator, and other RHOAI Go operators: builder stage compiles with FIPS flags (`CGO_ENABLED=1`, `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`); production stage copies the binary onto `ubi9/ubi-minimal`\n40\t- Add `rpms.lock.yaml` for RPM lockfile pinning and `go.sum` for Go dependency locking\n41\t- Apply the platform container security pattern: non-root execution (`USER 65532:65532` following the distroless convention), capability dropping (`capabilities.drop: [\"ALL\"]`), `seccompProfile.type: RuntimeDefault`\n42\t- Configure AMD64 builds as required for Tech Preview; include arm64 only if the pipeline supports it without additional effort\n43\t- Validate that the built image passes Konflux `check-payload` for FIPS compliance (binary linked against OpenSSL, no statically-linked Go crypto)\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- A Konflux component exists for the kagenti-operator image, built from the midstream fork, with a green build pipeline\n48\t- The image passes Konflux `check-payload` validation for FIPS compliance\n49\t- The Dockerfile follows the multi-stage FIPS pattern on a UBI9 base, with `rpms.lock.yaml` and `go.sum` present in the build context\n50\t- The container security requirements (non-root, dropped capabilities, RuntimeDefault seccomp) are satisfied in the image and manifests\n51\t- An AMD64 image is produced; arm64 status is recorded (included if free, otherwise deferred with rationale)\n52\t- The SHA256-pinned image reference is published for consumption by OLM/CSV packaging\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- [P0] Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation (`GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`, `CGO_ENABLED=1`) on UBI9 base (RFE acceptance criterion)\n57\t- [P2] Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required for TP; arm64 if pipeline supports it without additional effort)\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6132f1409369405","agent_id":"a7fb7d5324fc4e6ec","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"f8aaaf01-6d97-4b78-80c8-89b28643b