{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a09b32f614211842","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-A-E016\n3\ttitle: Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps for Tech Preview\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: add_remediation\n15\t  fallback_approach: Activated only if the upstream validation finds functional gaps.\n16\t    If the operator is fully functional, this epic is dropped; if gaps exceed two\n17\t    sprints of effort, negotiate TP scope reduction (defer MLflowReconciler and/or\n18\t    ClientRegistrationController) instead of full remediation.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: -1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Low\n32\tai_implementability_score: -1\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps for Tech Preview\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis conditional epic exists only if the upstream kagenti-operator validation finds functional gaps. It closes the identified gaps — missing or broken controllers (AgentRuntimeReconciler including the agent-card metadata fetch, MLflowReconciler, ClientRegistrationController), AgentRuntime CRD schema defects, or image-contract mismatches — in the upstream `kagenti/*` repositories first (upstream-first policy), then syncs the fixes into the `opendatahub-io` midstream fork so the Konflux-built images and pinned manifests pick them up.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Implement the remediation items enumerated in the upstream validation gap analysis, developed in the upstream `kagenti/kagenti-operator` repository first and then pulled into the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork\n44\t- Re-run the validation criteria from the gap analysis against the remediated operator\n45\t- Rebaseline the pinned midstream fork commit and rebuild the affected images so downstream productization consumes the fixed operator\n46\t- If the gap analysis recommends TP scope reduction instead of full remediation (gaps exceeding two sprints of effort), implement the agreed reduction (e.g., defer MLflowReconciler and/or ClientRegistrationController, disable the Keycloak-dependent controller) rather than closing the gaps\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- All gap-analysis remediation items are implemented upstream and synced to the midstream fork, or the agreed TP scope reduction is implemented and recorded\n51\t- The remediated (or scope-reduced) operator passes the validation criteria from the gap analysis\n52\t- The midstream fork pinned commit is rebaselined and the affected images rebuilt\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- [P0] Upstream-first policy: significant changes go to `kagenti/*` repos before being pulled into `opendatahub-io/*` midstream forks (RFE acceptance criterion)\n57\t- Supports the P0 Konflux-built operator image and DSC component HLRs by ensuring the productized operator is functional\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6132f1409369405","agent_id":"a7fb7d5324fc4e6ec","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"1da7798b-7282-476b-af88-dff381c69bea","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:28:15.891Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a09b32f614211842","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
