{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0a8303ed11b7f7e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 15\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n10\t\n11\tStrategy triage: **full decomposition** (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy is\n12\tL-effort (6-9 sprints), spans four strategy components (kagenti-operator, kagenti-extensions,\n13\trhods-operator, odh-dashboard) and five teams (Kagenti, Platform / ODH Operator, Dashboard, QE,\n14\tDocs). No Staff Engineer Input overrides (section contains template placeholder text only).\n15\t\n16\tThe strategy productizes an existing upstream operator: build-pipeline onboarding, DSC component\n17\tcontroller integration, OLM/CSV packaging, and dashboard BFF registration. Runtime agent\n18\tbehavior (registration, discovery, metadata sync) is explicitly out of scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589).\n19\t\n20\t## Epic List\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n23\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine the AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Determine TP dashboard integration depth for agent views | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Define AgentRuntime cleanup semantics when the kagenti component is disabled | Investigation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | Establish the kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | Establish the kagenti-extensions midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | License validation for kagenti-operator and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | License validation for kagenti-extensions and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P1 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 | Konflux build onboarding for the AuthBridge proxy sidecar image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E020 | KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E021 | OLM/CSV packaging for kagenti-operator with disconnected-install support | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E030 | Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E040 | E2E test plan and validation for the kagenti component lifecycle | Implementation | QE | P1 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E050 | Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the agent image contract | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P0 |\n39\t\n40\tBranch (conditional) epics — not standalone main-plan nodes; attached to their gating\n41\tInvestigation as plan documents:\n42\t\n43\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Gated by |\n44\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-A-E016 | Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps for Tech Preview | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E017 | Konflux onboarding for additional AuthBridge sidecar variants | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P2 | RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 |\n47\t\n48\tSizing note on E020 (controller workstream, strategy estimate 2-3 sprints): the epic intentionally\n49\tspans the whole component-controller change — component CRD, DSC CR schema extension, registry\n50\tregistration, action pipeline, kustomize manifest integration, cleanup-semantics implementation,\n51\tand RBAC coexistence verification — rather than splitting the skeleton from the pipeline/cleanup\n52\twork. All sub-deliverables land in one repo (rhods-operator) for one team following the\n53\t16-precedent component pattern, where they always ship as one registration; a skeleton-only epic\n54\twould not be independently shippable. The cleanup-semantics scope is bounded by the upstream\n55\tInvestigation decision, and the lifecycle E2E testing is carried by the QE epic. The full\n56\tjustification is recorded in E020's body (Sizing Justification section).\n57\t\n58\t## Dependency DAG\n59\t\n60\t```mermaid\n61\tgraph TD\n62\t    E001[\"E001 Upstream kagenti validation (Inv)\"]\n63\t    E002[\"E002 AuthBridge variant set (Inv)\"]\n64\t    E003[\"E003 Dashboard depth (Inv)\"]\n65\t    E004[\"E004 Cleanup semantics (Inv)\"]\n66\t    E010[\"E010 repo-onboarding kagenti-operator\"]\n67\t    E011[\"E011 repo-onboarding kagenti-extensions\"]\n68\t    E012[\"E012 license-validation kagenti-operator\"]\n69\t    E013[\"E013 license-validation kagenti-extensions\"]\n70\t    E014[\"E014 Konflux onboarding kagenti-operator image\"]\n71\t    E015[\"E015 Konflux onboarding AuthBridge proxy image\"]\n72\t    E020[\"E020 KagentiOperator DSC component controller\"]\n73\t    E021[\"E021 OLM/CSV packaging\"]\n74\t    E030[\"E030 Dashboard BFF plugin + feature flag\"]\n75\t    E040[\"E040 QE E2E lifecycle + disconnected validation\"]\n76\t    E050[\"E050 Documentation (docs-authoring)\"]\n77\t\n78\t    E010 --> E014\n79\t    E011 --> E015\n80\t    E004 --> E020\n81\t    E020 --> E021\n82\t    E003 --> E030\n83\t    E020 --> E040\n84\t    E021 --> E040\n85\t    E001 --> E050\n86\t    E010 --> E050\n87\t    E011 --> E050\n88\t    E012 --> E050\n89\t    E013 --> E050\n90\t    E014 --> E050\n91\t    E015 --> E050\n92\t    E020 --> E050\n93\t    E021 --> E050\n94\t    E030 --> E050\n95\t    E040 --> E050\n96\t\n97\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E016 Upstream gap remediation (conditional)\"]\n98\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E017 Additional AuthBridge variants (conditional)\"]\n99\t    E001 -.-> BA\n100\t    E002 -.-> BB\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\tSolid edges are main-plan dependencies (dependency must complete before dependent starts).\n104\tDashed edges are conditional branch activations: the branch epic exists only if the gating\n105\tInvestigation resolves to the outcome that requires it.\n106\t\n107\t## DAG Justification\n108\t\n109\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n110\t| --- | --- | --- |\n111\t| E010 → E014 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux component builds from the opendatahub-io midstream fork; the pipeline needs the repo. |\n112\t| E011 → E015 | Rule 5 | Same: the AuthBridge proxy image builds from the kagenti-extensions midstream fork. |\n113\t| E004 → E020 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementation) | Whether component cleanup includes cross-namespace CRD deletion or documents orphan semantics changes the controller's cleanup/finalizer scope. Bounded outcome → `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on E020. |\n114\t| E020 → E021 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The CSV declares the `KagentiOperator` CRD and the component controller's RBAC — artifacts produced by the controller work; packaging builds against them. |\n115\t| E003 → E030 | Rule 3 | Agent-list-as-tab (~1 sprint) vs standalone navigation section (~2 sprints) changes the BFF/UI scope of the dashboard epic. `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on E030. |\n116\t| E020 → E040 | Rule 13 | E2E lifecycle tests exercise the component controller's Managed/Removed behavior. |\n117\t| E021 → E040 | Rule 13 | Disconnected validation exercises the CSV `RELATED_IMAGE_*` mirroring path. |\n118\t| all Implementations → E050 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every main-plan Implementation epic. E001 is additionally included as a content dependency for the image-contract documentation; E050 records this as `gated_by` with `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` scoped to documentation content only (the epic's existence and structure do not depend on the outcome). Docs priority derived from strategy `priority: Critical` → P0 (docs-authoring priority exception; does not push P0 upstream). |\n119\t| E001 -.-> BRANCH-A-E016 | Rule 3 (conditional branch, add_remediation) | If the upstream operator has functional gaps, remediation work is added upstream-first. |\n120\t| E002 -.-> BRANCH-B-E017 | Rule 3 (conditional branch, remove) | If TP requires more than the authbridge-proxy variant, additional Konflux components are added. |\n121\t\n122\tDeliberately absent edges (anti-patterns per the rules):\n123\t\n124\t| Non-edge | Rule | Rationale |\n125\t| --- | --- | --- |\n126\t| E012/E013 → E014/E015 | Rules 7-8 | License validation runs in parallel with Konflux onboarding (independent inputs). |\n127\t| E014/E015 → E020/E021 | Rules 10, 13 | SHA256-pinned image digests consumed by the CSV (`RELATED_IMAGE_*`) are configuration references, not build-against artifacts — enforced as \"pinned digest available / pipeline green\" ACs on E020/E021, never as DAG edges. Konflux onboarding and the component controller must run in parallel. |\n128\t| E001 → E014 | Rule 14 + strategy risk direction | The strategy directs submitting the Konflux onboarding request immediately (lead-time risk) while upstream validation runs in sprint 1; the pipeline onboards whatever code exists at pinned commits. The validation outcome gates only the conditional remediation branch. |\n129\t| E020 → E030 | Rule 14 | Different repos with no shared build-against artifact: the dashboard BFF reads the upstream-defined AgentRuntime CRD and DSC component state (configuration references); coupling is enforced by an AC on E030, not an edge. |\n130\t| E010 → E020 | Rules 13-14 | The controller consumes midstream manifests at pinned commits — a configuration reference, gated by an AC on E020, not an edge. |\n131\t\n132\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n133\t\n134\t| HLR | Priority | Covering epics |\n135\t| --- | --- | --- |\n136\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 base | P0 | E014 (chain: E010, E012) |\n137\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern, `managementState: Managed/Removed` | P0 | E020 |\n138\t| When disabled (`Removed`), all operator-managed resources cleaned up | P0 | E020 (scope resolved by E004) |\n139\t| Upstream-first policy (changes land in `kagenti/*` before `opendatahub-io/*` midstream) | P0 | E010, E011 (sync process ACs); BRANCH-A-E016 if remediation is triggered |\n140\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E020 |\n141\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag | P1 | E030 (depth resolved by E003) |\n142\t| OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` for disconnected installation | P1 | E021 |\n143\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E015 (chain: E011, E013) |\n144\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if pipeline supports without extra effort) | P2 | E014, E015 (acceptance criteria — arm64 is opportunistic, not a separate deliverable) |\n145\t\n146\tStrategy-level acceptance criteria coverage: DSC enable/disable and cleanup ACs → E020/E040;\n147\tFIPS check-payload ACs → E014/E015; AgentRuntime label-application AC → E040 (E2E over the\n148\tdeployed operator); dashboard agent-list AC → E030; disconnected-install AC → E021/E040;\n149\tminimal-image-contract documentation MUST → E050. Runtime discovery/registration ACs at the top\n150\tof the strategy describe upstream operator behavior explicitly tracked out of scope\n151\t(RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589) and are validated, not built, by this decomposition (E040).\n152\t\n153\t## Investigation Handling of Strategy Unknowns\n154\t\n155\t| Strategy unknown | Disposition |\n156\t| --- | --- |\n157\t| Upstream kagenti-operator functional with all three controllers? (open question) | E001 Investigation — outcome can add remediation work (BRANCH-A-E016) or force TP scope reduction. |\n158\t| Does the operator require Keycloak as a runtime dependency; can ClientRegistrationController be disabled for TP? (open question) | Folded into E001 — resolved by the same experiment (exercising the upstream operator) and the same deliverable (gap analysis). |\n159\t| Minimal image contract for TP: A2A protocol format or simpler metadata format? (open question) | Technical half folded into E001 (what the operator actually consumes); documentation half is E050 content. Does not change which epics exist. |\n160\t| Which AuthBridge sidecar variants are needed for TP? (open question) | E002 Investigation — main plan ships the strategy's committed minimum (`authbridge-proxy`); additional variants are conditional BRANCH-B-E017. |\n161\t| Dashboard integration depth: tab vs standalone navigation? (open question) | E003 Investigation — gates E030 scope (`rewrite`). |\n162\t| What happens to user-namespace AgentRuntime CRs when the component is disabled? (open question) | E004 Investigation — gates E020 cleanup scope (`rewrite`). |\n163\t| Midstream fork set up and synced (assumption, needs validation) | E010/E011 — the repo-onboarding epics' own deliverable. |\n164\t| AgentRuntime CRD schema stable enough for TP (assumption, needs validation) | E001 (CRD stability assessment). |\n165\t| RBAC coexistence in `redhat-ods-applications` (assumption, needs validation) | E040 E2E coverage + E020 AC; risk-table mitigation. |\n166\t| OTEL trace sink MUST from parent RFE under team discussion (Open note on ACs) | Health warning — not in this strategy's scope or ACs; would add scope if confirmed. |\n167\t\n168\t## Component Mapping (canonical Jira components)\n169\t\n170\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n171\t| --- | --- | --- |\n172\t| kagenti-operator | Agentic | No kagenti-specific canonical component exists; all Kagenti-team epics (forks, license scans, Konflux onboarding, remediation) map to `Agentic`. |\n173\t| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | Same mapping; separate epics because they are separate strategy components/repos. |\n174\t| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | Closest canonical name for the core platform operator repo (paired with `AI Core Dashboard` below). |\n175\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Direct match. |\n176\t| QE (no owned component) | QE | Direct match. |\n177\t| Docs (no owned component) | Documentation | Direct match. |\n178\t\n179\tNew-component detection: neither kagenti-operator nor kagenti-extensions has an architecture\n180\tcontext file (only a tangential RBAC mention of `mcp.kagenti.com` in odh-dashboard.md), so both\n181\tget the full Rule 20 onboarding chain (repo-onboarding + license-validation in parallel →\n182\tkonflux-onboarding). No general implementation epic follows the chain: the strategy explicitly\n183\texcludes operator runtime development, so the chain's consumer is the rhods-operator component\n184\tcontroller (E020), which references manifests and image digests as configuration (ACs, not edges).\n185\t\n186\t## Conditional Branches\n187\t\n188\t- **BRANCH-A-E016** (gated by E001, `add_remediation`): activated only if the upstream\n189\t  validation finds functional gaps. If gaps exceed two sprints of effort, the fallback is TP\n190\t  scope reduction (defer MLflowReconciler and/or ClientRegistrationController) per the\n191\t  strategy's risk mitigation, not full remediation.\n192\t- **BRANCH-B-E017** (gated by E002, `remove`): activated only if TP requires AuthBridge\n193\t  variants beyond `authbridge-proxy`. If TP ships proxy-only, the epic is dropped and the\n194\t  variants defer to a later release.\n195\t\n196\tBranch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path.\n197\t\n198\t## Health Warnings\n199\t\n200\t- **OTEL trace sink (open scope risk):** the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) carries a MUST for\n201\t  OTEL trace sink integration \"not yet reflected here — under team discussion\". If confirmed,\n202\t  it adds scope beyond this decomposition (observability wiring was otherwise delegated to\n203\t  RHAIRFE-7589/ARC). Track the discussion outcome before release planning.\n204\t- **Process gates pending human review:** Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, Licence\n205\t  Validation, UXD Support, and Documentation Support are all \"Pending human review\" in the\n206\t  strategy's prerequisites table, and the issue carries `ac-review-pending` and\n207\t  `confidence-yellow` labels. The proposed acceptance criteria themselves are marked\n208\t  \"requires PM/Engineering validation\".\n209\t- **Konflux lead time (schedule risk, not an AC):** pipeline capacity \"needs submission\" and\n210\t  late submission risks the code-complete deadline. The onboarding request must be submitted\n211\t  immediately (tracked in E014/E015 scope and risks); escalation path per the strategy risk\n212\t  table (platform lead if <2 weeks before deadline).\n213\t- **Minor strategy typo:** proposed AC 3 references CRD `agentrimes.agent.kagenti.dev`\n214\t  (should be the AgentRuntime CRD name as defined upstream, `agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`).\n215\t- **Priority note:** the dashboard HLR is P1 while the operator productization is P0 —\n216\t  consistent with the strategy's TP framing (dashboard is \"basic visibility\" only). No\n217\t  inversion detected. P2 multi-arch is correctly opportunistic.\n218\t\n219\t## Tiered Delivery\n220\t\n221\tNot applicable. Both external dependencies (upstream kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions)\n222\talready exist in the `kagenti` GitHub org, and the internal dependencies (component registry\n223\tpattern, Module Federation infrastructure) are established. The only timing-uncertain\n224\tdependency is Konflux pipeline capacity, which is an internal process lead time handled inside\n225\tthe konflux-onboarding epics — not an upstream feature gate that would justify a Tier 1/Tier 2\n226\tvalue split. The conditional branches above are risk branches, not delivery tiers.\n227\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80d8b2e2dbd4618f","agent_id":"a718a47f9410d0a38","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"a4295bf1-b296-4098-a404-9f401668bf5d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:34:16.840Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0a8303ed11b7f7e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second revision of RHAISTRAT-8006"}
