{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9318b6897de8868a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 15\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n11\t\n12\tStrategy triage: **full decomposition** (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy is\n13\tL-effort (6-9 sprints), spans four strategy components (kagenti-operator, kagenti-extensions,\n14\trhods-operator, odh-dashboard) and five teams (Kagenti, Platform / ODH Operator, Dashboard, QE,\n15\tDocs). No Staff Engineer Input overrides (section contains template placeholder text only).\n16\t\n17\tThe strategy productizes an existing upstream operator: build-pipeline onboarding, DSC component\n18\tcontroller integration, OLM/CSV packaging, and dashboard BFF registration. Runtime agent\n19\tbehavior (registration, discovery, metadata sync) is explicitly out of scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589).\n20\t\n21\t## Epic List\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n24\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator readiness for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine the AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Determine TP dashboard integration depth for agent views | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Define AgentRuntime cleanup semantics when the kagenti component is disabled | Investigation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | Establish the kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | Establish the kagenti-extensions midstream fork under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | License validation for kagenti-operator and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | License validation for kagenti-extensions and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | Kagenti | P1 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | Konflux build onboarding for the kagenti-operator image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P0 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E015 | Konflux build onboarding for the AuthBridge proxy sidecar image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P1 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E020 | KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E021 | OLM/CSV packaging for kagenti-operator with disconnected-install support | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E030 | Dashboard BFF plugin and feature flag for agent views | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E040 | E2E test plan and validation for the kagenti component lifecycle | Implementation | QE | P1 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E050 | Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the agent image contract | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P0 |\n40\t\n41\tBranch (conditional) epics — not standalone main-plan nodes; attached to their gating\n42\tInvestigation as plan documents:\n43\t\n44\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Gated by |\n45\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-A-E016 | Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps for Tech Preview | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 | RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 |\n47\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E017 | Konflux onboarding for additional AuthBridge sidecar variants | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | Kagenti | P2 | RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 |\n48\t\n49\tSizing note on E020 (controller workstream, strategy estimate 2-3 sprints): the epic intentionally\n50\tspans the whole component-controller change — component CRD, DSC CR schema extension, registry\n51\tregistration, action pipeline, kustomize manifest integration, cleanup-semantics implementation,\n52\tand RBAC coexistence verification — rather than splitting the skeleton from the pipeline/cleanup\n53\twork. All sub-deliverables land in one repo (rhods-operator) for one team following the\n54\t16-precedent component pattern, where they always ship as one registration; a skeleton-only epic\n55\twould not be independently shippable. The cleanup-semantics scope is bounded by the upstream\n56\tInvestigation decision, and the lifecycle E2E testing is carried by the QE epic. The full\n57\tjustification is recorded in E020's body (Sizing Justification section).\n58\t\n59\t## Dependency DAG\n60\t\n61\t```mermaid\n62\tgraph TD\n63\t    E001[\"E001 Upstream kagenti validation (Inv)\"]\n64\t    E002[\"E002 AuthBridge variant set (Inv)\"]\n65\t    E003[\"E003 Dashboard depth (Inv)\"]\n66\t    E004[\"E004 Cleanup semantics (Inv)\"]\n67\t    E010[\"E010 repo-onboarding kagenti-operator\"]\n68\t    E011[\"E011 repo-onboarding kagenti-extensions\"]\n69\t    E012[\"E012 license-validation kagenti-operator\"]\n70\t    E013[\"E013 license-validation kagenti-extensions\"]\n71\t    E014[\"E014 Konflux onboarding kagenti-operator image\"]\n72\t    E015[\"E015 Konflux onboarding AuthBridge proxy image\"]\n73\t    E020[\"E020 KagentiOperator DSC component controller\"]\n74\t    E021[\"E021 OLM/CSV packaging\"]\n75\t    E030[\"E030 Dashboard BFF plugin + feature flag\"]\n76\t    E040[\"E040 QE E2E lifecycle + disconnected validation\"]\n77\t    E050[\"E050 Documentation (docs-authoring)\"]\n78\t\n79\t    E010 --> E014\n80\t    E011 --> E015\n81\t    E004 --> E020\n82\t    E020 --> E021\n83\t    E002 --> E021\n84\t    E003 --> E030\n85\t    E020 --> E040\n86\t    E021 --> E040\n87\t    E001 --> E050\n88\t    E010 --> E050\n89\t    E011 --> E050\n90\t    E012 --> E050\n91\t    E013 --> E050\n92\t    E014 --> E050\n93\t    E015 --> E050\n94\t    E020 --> E050\n95\t    E021 --> E050\n96\t    E030 --> E050\n97\t    E040 --> E050\n98\t\n99\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E016 Upstream gap remediation (conditional)\"]\n100\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E017 Additional AuthBridge variants (conditional)\"]\n101\t    E001 -.-> BA\n102\t    E002 -.-> BB\n103\t    E010 --> BA\n104\t    E014 --> BA\n105\t    E011 --> BB\n106\t```\n107\t\n108\tSolid edges are main-plan dependencies (dependency must complete before dependent starts).\n109\tDashed edges are conditional branch activations: the branch epic exists only if the gating\n110\tInvestigation resolves to the outcome that requires it. A branch epic's solid-edge\n111\tdependencies (E010/E014 → BRANCH-A-E016, E011 → BRANCH-B-E017) apply only when that branch\n112\tis activated: the remediation branch syncs into the midstream fork and rebuilds images\n113\tthrough the Konflux component, and the variant branch builds from the kagenti-extensions\n114\tmidstream fork, so both consume main-plan onboarding artifacts.\n115\t\n116\t## DAG Justification\n117\t\n118\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n119\t| --- | --- | --- |\n120\t| E010 → E014 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | The Konflux component builds from the opendatahub-io midstream fork; the pipeline needs the repo. |\n121\t| E011 → E015 | Rule 5 | Same: the AuthBridge proxy image builds from the kagenti-extensions midstream fork. |\n122\t| E004 → E020 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementation) | Whether component cleanup includes cross-namespace CRD deletion or documents orphan semantics changes the controller's cleanup/finalizer scope. Bounded outcome → `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on E020. |\n123\t| E020 → E021 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The CSV declares the `KagentiOperator` CRD and the component controller's RBAC — artifacts produced by the controller work; packaging builds against them. |\n124\t| E002 → E021 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementation) | E021 conditionally adds `RELATED_IMAGE_*` CSV entries for additional AuthBridge variants based on the variant-set decision — a main-plan consumption of the E002 outcome, so it must be gated, not merely conditioned in prose. `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on E021: proxy-only narrows the entry set to the committed minimum; additional variants extend it (digests via configuration-reference ACs, not edges). |\n125\t| E003 → E030 | Rule 3 | Agent-list-as-tab (~1 sprint) vs standalone navigation section (~2 sprints) changes the BFF/UI scope of the dashboard epic. `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on E030. |\n126\t| E020 → E040 | Rule 13 | E2E lifecycle tests exercise the component controller's Managed/Removed behavior. |\n127\t| E021 → E040 | Rule 13 | Disconnected validation exercises the CSV `RELATED_IMAGE_*` mirroring path. |\n128\t| all Implementations → E050 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every main-plan Implementation epic. E001 is additionally included as a content dependency for the image-contract documentation; E050 records this as `gated_by` with `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` scoped to documentation content only (the epic's existence and structure do not depend on the outcome). Docs priority derived from strategy `priority: Critical` → P0 (docs-authoring priority exception; does not push P0 upstream). |\n129\t| E001 -.-> BRANCH-A-E016 | Rule 3 (conditional branch, add_remediation) | If the upstream operator has functional gaps, remediation work is added upstream-first. |\n130\t| E002 -.-> BRANCH-B-E017 | Rule 3 (conditional branch, remove) | If TP requires more than the authbridge-proxy variant, additional Konflux components are added. |\n131\t| E010 → BRANCH-A-E016 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The remediation syncs fixes into the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork and rebaselines its pinned commit — artifacts the repo-onboarding epic establishes. Edge applies only when the branch is activated. |\n132\t| E014 → BRANCH-A-E016 | Rule 13 | The affected images are rebuilt through the kagenti-operator Konflux component; the rebuild cannot run before the pipeline exists. Edge applies only when the branch is activated. |\n133\t| E011 → BRANCH-B-E017 | Rule 5 (repo-onboarding → konflux-onboarding serial) | Same as E011 → E015: the additional variants build from the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions` midstream fork the repo-onboarding epic establishes. Edge applies only when the branch is activated. |\n134\t\n135\tDeliberately absent edges (anti-patterns per the rules):\n136\t\n137\t| Non-edge | Rule | Rationale |\n138\t| --- | --- | --- |\n139\t| E012/E013 → E014/E015 | Rules 7-8 | License validation runs in parallel with Konflux onboarding (independent inputs). |\n140\t| E014/E015 → E020/E021 | Rules 10, 13 | SHA256-pinned image digests consumed by the CSV (`RELATED_IMAGE_*`) are configuration references, not build-against artifacts — enforced as \"pinned digest available / pipeline green\" ACs on E020/E021, never as DAG edges. Konflux onboarding and the component controller must run in parallel. |\n141\t| E001 → E014 | Rule 14 + strategy risk direction | The strategy directs submitting the Konflux onboarding request immediately (lead-time risk) while upstream validation runs in sprint 1; the pipeline onboards whatever code exists at pinned commits. The validation outcome gates only the conditional remediation branch. |\n142\t| E020 → E030 | Rule 14 | Different repos with no shared build-against artifact: the dashboard BFF reads the upstream-defined AgentRuntime CRD and DSC component state (configuration references); coupling is enforced by an AC on E030, not an edge. |\n143\t| E010 → E020 | Rules 13-14 | The controller consumes midstream manifests at pinned commits — a configuration reference, gated by an AC on E020, not an edge. |\n144\t\n145\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n146\t\n147\t| HLR | Priority | Covering epics |\n148\t| --- | --- | --- |\n149\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 base | P0 | E014 (chain: E010, E012) |\n150\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern, `managementState: Managed/Removed` | P0 | E020 |\n151\t| When disabled (`Removed`), all operator-managed resources cleaned up | P0 | E020 (scope resolved by E004) |\n152\t| Upstream-first policy (changes land in `kagenti/*` before `opendatahub-io/*` midstream) | P0 | E010, E011 (sync process ACs); BRANCH-A-E016 if remediation is triggered |\n153\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E020 |\n154\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag | P1 | E030 (depth resolved by E003) |\n155\t| OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` for disconnected installation | P1 | E021 (owns the entries for all variants; additional-variant entries gated by E002) |\n156\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E015 (chain: E011, E013) |\n157\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if pipeline supports without extra effort) | P2 | E014, E015 (acceptance criteria — arm64 is opportunistic, not a separate deliverable) |\n158\t\n159\tStrategy-level acceptance criteria coverage: DSC enable/disable and cleanup ACs → E020/E040;\n160\tFIPS check-payload ACs → E014/E015; AgentRuntime label-application AC → E040 (E2E over the\n161\tdeployed operator); dashboard agent-list AC → E030; disconnected-install AC → E021/E040;\n162\tminimal-image-contract documentation MUST → E050. Runtime discovery/registration ACs at the top\n163\tof the strategy describe upstream operator behavior explicitly tracked out of scope\n164\t(RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589) and are validated, not built, by this decomposition (E040).\n165\t\n166\t## Investigation Handling of Strategy Unknowns\n167\t\n168\t| Strategy unknown | Disposition |\n169\t| --- | --- |\n170\t| Upstream kagenti-operator functional with all three controllers? (open question) | E001 Investigation — outcome can add remediation work (BRANCH-A-E016) or force TP scope reduction. |\n171\t| Does the operator require Keycloak as a runtime dependency; can ClientRegistrationController be disabled for TP? (open question) | Folded into E001 — resolved by the same experiment (exercising the upstream operator) and the same deliverable (gap analysis). |\n172\t| Minimal image contract for TP: A2A protocol format or simpler metadata format? (open question) | Technical half folded into E001 (what the operator actually consumes); documentation half is E050 content. Does not change which epics exist. |\n173\t| Which AuthBridge sidecar variants are needed for TP? (open question) | E002 Investigation — main plan ships the strategy's committed minimum (`authbridge-proxy`); additional variants are conditional BRANCH-B-E017, and the additional `RELATED_IMAGE_*` CSV entries in E021 are gated on the same decision. |\n174\t| Dashboard integration depth: tab vs standalone navigation? (open question) | E003 Investigation — gates E030 scope (`rewrite`). |\n175\t| What happens to user-namespace AgentRuntime CRs when the component is disabled? (open question) | E004 Investigation — gates E020 cleanup scope (`rewrite`). |\n176\t| Midstream fork set up and synced (assumption, needs validation) | E010/E011 — the repo-onboarding epics' own deliverable. |\n177\t| AgentRuntime CRD schema stable enough for TP (assumption, needs validation) | E001 (CRD stability assessment). |\n178\t| RBAC coexistence in `redhat-ods-applications` (assumption, needs validation) | E040 E2E coverage + E020 AC; risk-table mitigation. |\n179\t| OTEL trace sink MUST from parent RFE under team discussion (Open note on ACs) | Health warning — not in this strategy's scope or ACs; would add scope if confirmed. |\n180\t\n181\t## Component Mapping (canonical Jira components)\n182\t\n183\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n184\t| --- | --- | --- |\n185\t| kagenti-operator | Agentic | No kagenti-specific canonical component exists; all Kagenti-team epics (forks, license scans, Konflux onboarding, remediation) map to `Agentic`. |\n186\t| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | Same mapping; separate epics because they are separate strategy components/repos. |\n187\t| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | Closest canonical name for the core platform operator repo (paired with `AI Core Dashboard` below). |\n188\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Direct match. |\n189\t| QE (no owned component) | QE | Direct match. |\n190\t| Docs (no owned component) | Documentation | Direct match. |\n191\t\n192\tNew-component detection: neither kagenti-operator nor kagenti-extensions has an architecture\n193\tcontext file (only a tangential RBAC mention of `mcp.kagenti.com` in odh-dashboard.md), so both\n194\tget the full Rule 20 onboarding chain (repo-onboarding + license-validation in parallel →\n195\tkonflux-onboarding). No general implementation epic follows the chain: the strategy explicitly\n196\texcludes operator runtime development, so the chain's consumer is the rhods-operator component\n197\tcontroller (E020), which references manifests and image digests as configuration (ACs, not edges).\n198\t\n199\t## Conditional Branches\n200\t\n201\t- **BRANCH-A-E016** (gated by E001, `add_remediation`): activated only if the upstream\n202\t  validation finds functional gaps. When activated, it additionally depends on the\n203\t  kagenti-operator repo onboarding (the midstream fork it syncs into and rebaselines) and\n204\t  the kagenti-operator Konflux onboarding (the pipeline that rebuilds the affected images).\n205\t  If gaps exceed two sprints of effort, the fallback is TP scope reduction (defer\n206\t  MLflowReconciler and/or ClientRegistrationController) per the strategy's risk mitigation,\n207\t  not full remediation.\n208\t- **BRANCH-B-E017** (gated by E002, `remove`): activated only if TP requires AuthBridge\n209\t  variants beyond `authbridge-proxy`. When activated, it additionally depends on the\n210\t  kagenti-extensions repo onboarding (the midstream fork it builds from). The branch builds\n211\t  and publishes the SHA256-pinned image references for the additional variants; the\n212\t  `RELATED_IMAGE_*` CSV entries consuming them are owned by E021, which is gated on the same\n213\t  E002 decision, so the conditional packaging work has exactly one correctly-dependent owner.\n214\t  If TP ships proxy-only, the epic is dropped and the variants defer to a later release.\n215\t\n216\tBranch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path.\n217\t\n218\t## Health Warnings\n219\t\n220\t- **OTEL trace sink (open scope risk):** the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) carries a MUST for\n221\t  OTEL trace sink integration \"not yet reflected here — under team discussion\". If confirmed,\n222\t  it adds scope beyond this decomposition (observability wiring was otherwise delegated to\n223\t  RHAIRFE-7589/ARC). Track the discussion outcome before release planning.\n224\t- **Process gates pending human review:** Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, Licence\n225\t  Validation, UXD Support, and Documentation Support are all \"Pending human review\" in the\n226\t  strategy's prerequisites table, and the issue carries `ac-review-pending` and\n227\t  `confidence-yellow` labels. The proposed acceptance criteria themselves are marked\n228\t  \"requires PM/Engineering validation\".\n229\t- **Konflux lead time (schedule risk, not an AC):** pipeline capacity \"needs submission\" and\n230\t  late submission risks the code-complete deadline. The onboarding request must be submitted\n231\t  immediately (tracked in E014/E015 scope and risks); escalation path per the strategy risk\n232\t  table (platform lead if <2 weeks before deadline).\n233\t- **Minor strategy typo:** proposed AC 3 references CRD `agentrimes.agent.kagenti.dev`\n234\t  (should be the AgentRuntime CRD name as defined upstream, `agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`).\n235\t- **Priority note:** the dashboard HLR is P1 while the operator productization is P0 —\n236\t  consistent with the strategy's TP framing (dashboard is \"basic visibility\" only). No\n237\t  inversion detected. P2 multi-arch is correctly opportunistic.\n238\t\n239\t## Tiered Delivery\n240\t\n241\tNot applicable. Both external dependencies (upstream kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions)\n242\talready exist in the `kagenti` GitHub org, and the internal dependencies (component registry\n243\tpattern, Module Federation infrastructure) are established. The only timing-uncertain\n244\tdependency is Konflux pipeline capacity, which is an internal process lead time handled inside\n245\tthe konflux-onboarding epics — not an upstream feature gate that would justify a Tier 1/Tier 2\n246\tvalue split. The conditional branches above are risk branches, not delivery tiers.\n247\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-938922a3c6f81d8a","agent_id":"aaab2f6cf940fe815","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"85846cbe-b349-476b-9cf4-7f6a4cb50a40","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:38:36.973Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9318b6897de8868a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after second revision"}
