{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-90067edae6d13d29","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n3\ttitle: Determine TP dashboard integration depth for agent views\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Determine TP dashboard integration depth for agent views\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation decides how the Tech Preview agent views are surfaced in the OpenShift AI dashboard: as a tab within an existing project view (roughly one sprint of effort) or as a standalone navigation section (roughly two sprints). The answer changes the scope of the dashboard BFF plugin and React UI work, and it requires a UX design direction for the agent list view before implementation starts. The deliverable is a PM/UX decision with a design direction that the dashboard implementation can build against.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Decide, with PM and UX input, the Tech Preview integration depth: agent list as a tab in an existing project view vs a standalone navigation section\n34\t- Produce a UX design direction for the TP agent list view (list AgentRuntime CRs, show status, link to workload details — read-only; full agent management UI is out of scope)\n35\t- Record the decision with rationale and the effort implication for the dashboard implementation\n36\t\n37\t## Acceptance Criteria\n38\t\n39\t- A decision record exists fixing the TP integration depth (tab vs standalone section), with PM/UX sign-off\n40\t- A UX design direction for the agent list view exists that covers the TP scope: list of AgentRuntime CRs from user-accessible namespaces, status display, and links to workload details\n41\t\n42\t## HLR Traceability\n43\t\n44\tNo HLR is directly delivered. This investigation fixes the scope of the P1 HLR \"Dashboard\n45\tintegration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag for agent views\".\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-938922a3c6f81d8a","agent_id":"aaab2f6cf940fe815","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"7519b9aa-1cac-483e-9044-16d43d5af217","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:38:42.149Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90067edae6d13d29","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after second revision"}
