{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e17e0433e7a95d7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n3\ttitle: Define AgentRuntime cleanup semantics when the kagenti component is disabled\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Define AgentRuntime cleanup semantics when the kagenti component is disabled\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation decides what happens to user-created AgentRuntime CRs in user namespaces when the kagenti-operator component is disabled in the Data Science Cluster CR (`managementState: Removed`). The component controller's standard cleanup covers operator-managed resources in `redhat-ods-applications` (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration, namespace-scoped resources), but user-created CRs in other namespaces may become orphaned. The open question is whether the cleanup should include cross-namespace CRD deletion or whether orphan semantics are documented instead. The answer changes the cleanup/finalizer scope of the component controller implementation. The deliverable is a documented cleanup-semantics decision consistent with the platform's garbage-collection pattern.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Determine the behavior of user-created AgentRuntime CRs in user namespaces when the component transitions to `Removed` (operator no longer running to reconcile them)\n34\t- Decide the cleanup scope: operator-managed resources only (with documented orphan behavior for user CRs) vs cleanup that also enumerates and deletes user-created CRs cross-namespace (e.g., via an explicit finalizer on the component CR)\n35\t- Survey the cleanup and finalizer patterns of the existing component controllers in the rhods-operator component registry for precedent\n36\t- Record the decision with rationale, including the resource-cleanup inventory (controller Deployment; ClusterRoles/ClusterRoleBindings/Roles/RoleBindings; the AgentRuntime CRD; the mutating webhook configuration; ConfigMaps/Secrets in `redhat-ods-applications`)\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A decision record exists fixing the disable-cleanup semantics (operator-managed-only vs including user-created CRs), with rationale grounded in existing component-controller precedent\n41\t- The full cleanup inventory is enumerated, matching the strategy's resource-cleanup non-functional requirement\n42\t- If cross-namespace cleanup is chosen, a finalizer design outline is included; if not, the documented orphan behavior for user CRs is specified\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\tNo HLR is directly delivered. This investigation fixes the scope of the P0 HLR \"When disabled\n47\t(`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed resources are cleaned up\".\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-938922a3c6f81d8a","agent_id":"aaab2f6cf940fe815","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"b44f0ecb-ccbc-44f2-9954-3d0a5c4a4e51","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:38:42.830Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e17e0433e7a95d7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after second revision"}
