{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99404856e3ed7f69","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n3\ttitle: Establish the kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: repo-onboarding\n10\tdependencies: null\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Establish the kagenti-operator midstream fork under opendatahub-io\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic establishes (or verifies and repairs) the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork of the upstream `kagenti/kagenti-operator` repository, and sets up the fork-sync process that all downstream productization work builds from. Konflux builds, kustomize manifest consumption, and license scanning all target this fork. The strategy's dependency table lists the fork as existing but its assumptions flag its sync state as needing validation, so this epic's deliverable covers both cases.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Verify the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork exists and is synced with upstream `kagenti/kagenti-operator`; create it if absent\n38\t- Establish and document the fork sync process (how upstream releases/commits are pulled into midstream)\n39\t- Document the upstream-first workflow required by the RFE: significant changes land in the `kagenti/*` upstream repos first, then are pulled into the `opendatahub-io/*` midstream forks — never developed midstream-only\n40\t- Identify the initial pinned commit of the fork that downstream consumers (build pipeline, component manifests) will reference\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- The `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork exists and its content is synced with the upstream repository at an identifiable pinned commit\n45\t- The fork sync process is documented and repeatable\n46\t- The upstream-first contribution workflow is documented for the Kagenti team\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- [P0] Upstream-first policy: significant changes go to `kagenti/*` repos before being pulled into `opendatahub-io/*` midstream forks (RFE acceptance criterion)\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-938922a3c6f81d8a","agent_id":"aaab2f6cf940fe815","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"d0d3c8f9-095e-4df7-8dc2-b26ca837a67a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:38:45.932Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-99404856e3ed7f69","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after second revision"}
