operators: builder stage compiles with FIPS flags (`CGO_ENABLED=1`, `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`); production stage copies the binary onto `ubi9/ubi-minimal`\n40\t- Add `rpms.lock.yaml` for RPM lockfile pinning and `go.sum` for Go dependency locking\n41\t- Apply the platform container security pattern: non-root execution (`USER 65532:65532` following the distroless convention), capability dropping (`capabilities.drop: [\"ALL\"]`), `seccompProfile.type: RuntimeDefault`\n42\t- Configure AMD64 builds as required for Tech Preview; include arm64 only if the pipeline supports it without additional effort\n43\t- Validate that the built image passes Konflux `check-payload` for FIPS compliance (binary linked against OpenSSL, no statically-linked Go crypto)\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- A Konflux component exists for the kagenti-operator image, built from the midstream fork, with a green build pipeline\n48\t- The image passes Konflux `check-payload` validation for FIPS compliance\n49\t- The Dockerfile follows the multi-stage FIPS pattern on a UBI9 base, with `rpms.lock.yaml` and `go.sum` present in the build context\n50\t- The container security requirements (non-root, dropped capabilities, RuntimeDefault seccomp) are satisfied in the image and manifests\n51\t- An AMD64 image is produced; arm64 status is recorded (included if free, otherwise deferred with rationale)\n52\t- The SHA256-pinned image reference is published for consumption by OLM/CSV packaging\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- [P0] Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation (`GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`, `CGO_ENABLED=1`) on UBI9 base (RFE acceptance criterion)\n57\t- [P2] Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required for TP; arm64 if pipeline supports it without additional effort)\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-938922a3c6f81d8a","agent_id":"aaab2f6cf940fe815","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"af7effe9-5053-4564-90fa-ffcc82e83