{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80c0b7bafc278faa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E050\n3\ttitle: Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the agent image contract\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: Docs\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E011\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E012\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E013\n16\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E014\n17\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E015\n18\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E020\n19\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E021\n20\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E030\n21\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E040\n22\tai_signals:\n23\t  change_specificity: 1\n24\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n25\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n26\t  existing_foundation: 1\n27\t  open_questions: -1\n28\t  external_dependency: 0\n29\t  human_process_gates: -1\n30\t  repo_access: 1\n31\t  architecture_claims: 0\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: Medium\n34\tai_implementability_score: 2\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\tbranch: null\n37\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n38\tgate_failure_impact:\n39\t  action: rewrite\n40\t  fallback_approach: 'Content dependency, not a structural gate: E001 does not change\n41\t    this epic''s existence or structure, only its content. If the upstream validation\n42\t    finds functional gaps or forces a TP scope reduction, the minimal image contract\n43\t    and agent onboarding documentation is rewritten against the remediated or scope-reduced\n44\t    operator behavior; the DSC enablement and disconnected-installation content is\n45\t    unaffected.'\n46\t---\n47\t# Documentation for kagenti-operator enablement and the agent image contract\n48\t\n49\t## Description\n50\t\n51\tThis epic authors the customer-facing documentation for the kagenti-operator Tech Preview: installation and upgrade documentation for enabling the component via the Data Science Cluster CR, and the minimal image contract documentation that tells customers how to build a discoverable agent image. This is substantive new content authoring in the Red Hat docs content process, and it runs last so the docs describe what was actually built.\n52\t\n53\t## Scope\n54\t\n55\tContent outline (to be authored inside the Red Hat docs toolchain):\n56\t\n57\t- **Enabling the kagenti-operator (installation):** how to enable the component via the DSC CR (`managementState: Managed`), the Tech Preview opt-in default (`Removed`), what gets deployed (operator, CRDs, RBAC, webhook in `redhat-ods-applications`), and how to disable it (`managementState: Removed`) with the resulting resource cleanup behavior, including the documented behavior of user-created AgentRuntime CRs\n58\t- **Minimal agent image contract:** how to build an agent image any framework can use — the capability description endpoint format (per the validated metadata format the operator consumes), health check expectations, and card structure (endpoint, health check, card fields), based on the upstream validation findings\n59\t- **Onboarding an agent:** creating an AgentRuntime CR that selects an existing Deployment (targetRef selection), and what the platform then does (registration, discoverability, console visibility) at Tech Preview scope\n60\t- **Disconnected installation:** mirroring the kagenti-operator and AuthBridge images for air-gapped clusters via the `RELATED_IMAGE_*` mechanism\n61\t- **Upgrade notes:** TP maturity caveats and the absence of backwards-compatibility concerns (new component, disabled by default)\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Installation and enablement documentation covers DSC-based enablement and disablement, including the cleanup behavior on disable\n66\t- The minimal image contract documentation covers endpoint format, health check, and card structure, matching the validated contract the operator enforces\n67\t- Agent onboarding documentation covers AgentRuntime CR creation via targetRef selection\n68\t- Disconnected-installation documentation covers image mirroring via `RELATED_IMAGE_*`\n69\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implementation before publication\n70\t- Content is published through the Red Hat docs content process for the Tech Preview release\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\tNo numbered HLR covers documentation. This epic delivers the strategy-level MUST acceptance\n75\tcriterion \"Documentation covers the minimal image contract for creating a discoverable agent\n76\t(endpoint format, health check, card structure)\" and the Docs team commitment (installation and\n77\tupgrade documentation for enabling kagenti-operator via DSC).\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-938922a3c6f81d8a","agent_id":"aaab2f6cf940fe815","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"6dde7165-4371-4592-b1ac-608c1c244ce0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:38:58.541Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80c0b7bafc278faa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after second revision"}
