{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b45a8fc4971f6d4d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-A-E016\n3\ttitle: Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps for Tech Preview\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E014\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: add_remediation\n17\t  fallback_approach: Activated only if the upstream validation finds functional gaps.\n18\t    If the operator is fully functional, this epic is dropped; if gaps exceed two\n19\t    sprints of effort, negotiate TP scope reduction (defer MLflowReconciler and/or\n20\t    ClientRegistrationController) instead of full remediation.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: -1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: -1\n27\t  external_dependency: -1\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 0\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: Low\n34\tai_implementability_score: -1\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Close upstream kagenti-operator functional gaps for Tech Preview\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tThis conditional epic exists only if the upstream kagenti-operator validation finds functional gaps. It closes the identified gaps — missing or broken controllers (AgentRuntimeReconciler including the agent-card metadata fetch, MLflowReconciler, ClientRegistrationController), AgentRuntime CRD schema defects, or image-contract mismatches — in the upstream `kagenti/*` repositories first (upstream-first policy), then syncs the fixes into the `opendatahub-io` midstream fork so the Konflux-built images and pinned manifests pick them up.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Implement the remediation items enumerated in the upstream validation gap analysis, developed in the upstream `kagenti/kagenti-operator` repository first and then pulled into the `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork\n46\t- Re-run the validation criteria from the gap analysis against the remediated operator\n47\t- Rebaseline the pinned midstream fork commit and rebuild the affected images so downstream productization consumes the fixed operator\n48\t- If the gap analysis recommends TP scope reduction instead of full remediation (gaps exceeding two sprints of effort), implement the agreed reduction (e.g., defer MLflowReconciler and/or ClientRegistrationController, disable the Keycloak-dependent controller) rather than closing the gaps\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- All gap-analysis remediation items are implemented upstream and synced to the midstream fork, or the agreed TP scope reduction is implemented and recorded\n53\t- The remediated (or scope-reduced) operator passes the validation criteria from the gap analysis\n54\t- The midstream fork pinned commit is rebaselined and the affected images rebuilt\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P0] Upstream-first policy: significant changes go to `kagenti/*` repos before being pulled into `opendatahub-io/*` midstream forks (RFE acceptance criterion)\n59\t- Supports the P0 Konflux-built operator image and DSC component HLRs by ensuring the productized operator is functional\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-938922a3c6f81d8a","agent_id":"aaab2f6cf940fe815","session_id":"e32792c3-9f26-4396-a9d5-fe6ebf0cdb37","uuid":"2feccd1b-7128-4af2-8808-d4f013c575ca","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:38:59.178Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b45a8fc4971f6d4d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review after second revision"}
